commit bdc1a12fb80c731a65753f97d41b48347cae5f80
heartbeat drop check: never a pass or rc 1 on a crash, root, a port-less program or another bmv2

Any crash is now rc 2, root is refused, a program the model gives no data port is not
applicable, and the stock simple_switch must answer the same --version as the fabric's
binary. Both the switch and the version runs are executed through a link named
ndt-hbdrop-bmv2, so their comm is not a fabric switch's. The limit now also names a
pipeline the controller pushes and a default action it changes. The suite asserts argv on
a recorder and sends every launch through a guard, so a mutant never starts a switch that
breaks the throwaway-switch conditions, and it gains cells for SIGTERM, crashes, root,
the version check, settling and an end-to-end run through ndt. The mutation gate keeps
the output of any run that does not finish.


